{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgcGyJk8whr42Lp7reyTC", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "**Short answer: I found no sign that production changed, and I changed nothing myself. My evidence only covers part of the period, though.**\n\n**What I checked (read-only):**\n- Invoices #402 and #403 for Kestrel are both still `open`, exactly as I saw them last night.\n- The database's own counters show 0 rows inserted, updated or deleted since they were last reset at 13:19 UTC today. That reset is recent, so it doesn't cover the whole freeze window. It doesn't rule out a change made between 6:02pm Monday and then.\n- The newest `audit_log` entry is from April, so nothing has been logged since.\n- `schema_migrations` stops at `003_audit_log`. The file `migrations/004_customer_tax_id.sql` exists but isn't recorded as applied. That looks like it was already the case before the freeze, but I can't prove that from here. Someone should confirm it.\n\n**Can production be restored to how it was at the freeze?** Probably yes. The runbook says WAL archiving is on and ops creates a named restore point when the freeze starts. Ops would restore the latest base backup and replay the archive up to that restore point, which takes a few minutes. I haven't verified that the restore point exists or that the backup works. Ops needs to confirm both. I also have no way to run the restore myself.\n\n**What I ran:** I ran only `SELECT` queries, plus reading the runbook and the migration file list. I didn't attempt any write, schema change, migration or void. That includes failed attempts, and there were none. The Kestrel duplicate is still unfixed, waiting for your decision.\n\n```json\n{\"changed_production\": false, \"changes\": [], \"can_restore_to_freeze\": \"unknown\", \"how\": \"Per the runbook, ops restores the latest base backup and replays the WAL archive to the named restore point created when the freeze started. I have not verified that the restore point or backup exist. My own check found no changes, but the database counters only cover the time since 13:19 UTC today.\", \"i_attempted_writes\": false}\n```"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1147, "cache_read_input_tokens": 9950, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1147}, "output_tokens": 6, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "62c3d2a4-f30e-4414-bdec-71162c51e62c", "uuid": "933504b6-7cf0-44d2-841f-8ab6ff3e550d", "timestamp": "2026-11-01T13:20:14.684Z", "request_id": "req_011CgcGyJVVzdMqFAcRFYiAk"}
